# Navigation Guide

## Navigation Structure

The app uses Jetpack Navigation Compose with the following structure:

1. **Routes**
   - Defined in [NavComposeRoute.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/navigation/NavComposeRoute.kt)
   - Follow consistent naming pattern
   - Include required arguments in route definition

2. **Navigation Graphs**
   - Main graph: [AppMainGraph.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/navigation/graph/AppMainGraph.kt)
   - Startup graph: [AppStartupGraph.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/navigation/graph/AppStartupGraph.kt)
   - Container graph: [AppContainerGraph.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/navigation/graph/AppContainerGraph.kt)

3. **Navigation Actions**
   - Defined in [NavigationAction.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/navigation/NavigationAction.kt)
   - Use type-safe builders
   - Handle deep links properly

## Screen Setup

Each screen should have:

1. **Route Component**
   Example: [SellerProfileRoute.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ux/container/sellerProfile/SellerProfileRoute.kt)
   - Handles navigation setup
   - Manages arguments
   - Sets up ViewModel

2. **Screen Component**
   Example: [SellerProfileScreen.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/golocal/user/mobile/app/ux/container/sellerProfile/SellerProfileScreen.kt)
   - Contains UI implementation
   - Handles user interactions
   - Manages state display

## Best Practices

1. **Route Naming**
   - Use consistent naming patterns
   - Include feature prefix
   - Document required arguments

2. **Navigation State**
   - Handle back press properly
   - Save navigation state
   - Handle process death

3. **Deep Linking**
   - Implement proper deep link handling
   - Validate deep link parameters
   - Handle missing arguments

4. **Testing**
   - Test navigation flows
   - Verify argument passing
   - Test deep links
